        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 8:50 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Tuesday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for Eastern Ontario. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Renfrew, Arnprior and Calabogie. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:EC-MSC-SMC:1.1:Designation_Code</valueName>
            <value>ON_00_01_LAND</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:2.0:WirelessImmediate</valueName>
            <value>Yes</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:2.0:WirelessText</valueName>
            <value>Environment Canada: TORNADO in this mobile coverage area.
Take immediate cover in a basement or interior room if weather threat approaches. Shelter from flying debris if outside.
Tornado Warning, 8:50 p.m. EDT Tuesday 30 June
</value>
